{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_016XbUcL1ysZ8LbbcvN4Bk4W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything is complete, verified, and committed. I'm freezing here with ~19 min of safety buffer rather than risk a run being hard-killed mid-execution.\n\n## Final summary\n\n**Best fineweb val_loss: `3.8125`** (5-min, single-GPU) — down from the baseline **4.1955** (−0.383).\n\n### What I found\nThe box actually exposed **only 1 H100**, so all runs were sequential (one single-GPU run at a time), and I budgeted accordingly. Two levers drove essentially all the improvement, both flowing from the same insight — in a 5-min budget the 124M model is **massively undertrained (~1 token/param)**, so loss is bottlenecked by compute, not capacity:\n\n1. **Global batch 512 → 64** (drop the 8-way grad accumulation): more optimizer steps over the same tokens → **4.1955 → 3.862** (−0.33). Benefit saturates by batch ≈128 (128 and 64 tie).\n2. **Depth 12 → 6 layers**: a smaller, faster model trains on more tokens and wins. Depth is **U-shaped with a clean minimum at 6** (12:3.862, 8:3.825, **6:3.816**, 5:3.824, 4:3.839 — 4L hits a capacity floor).\n\nLearning rate and warmdown fraction were both ~insensitive (verified by sweeps).\n\n### Deliverables (all committed on `claude-code-autonomous`)\n- **`exp/best.py`** — the winning config (6 layers, batch 64), identical to `exp/arch_l6.py`.\n- **Reproduce:** `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 torchrun --standalone --nproc_per_node=1 exp/best.py`\n- **Proof:** `logs/best_verify.out` (clean re-run → **3.8125**) and `logs/arch_l6.out` (original → 3.8158); the ~0.003 gap is init-seed noise, confirming robustness.\n- **`REPORT.md`** (narrative + plots), **`RESULTS.md`** (full sorted table), **`img/trajectories.png`** & **`img/final_bar.png`**.\n\nOne process-note for the human reading the history: chained \"wait-then-launch\" background commands repeatedly self-matched in `pgrep -f` (their own command line contains the script name), causing a few stalls — none corrupted any reported number; every counted val_loss came from a clean, isolated single-GPU run."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2064,"cache_read_input_tokens":153853,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2064},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e29014b2-1650-4138-bd86-b977ffa47697","uuid":"bb2d1108-11ee-482d-a761-e4195d42b927","request_id":"req_011CbimA1GeN3fmhm4iL1KHB"}
